 "result": "I created two files and haven't built or run the image, so it is untested.\n\n- `Dockerfile` is a multi-stage build.\n  - **Build stage:** `golang:1.27-alpine` builds `wings.go` into a static binary. CGO is off because the SQLite driver is pure Go. The build also sets `system.Version` through `-ldflags`, as the Makefile does.\n  - **Runtime stage:** `alpine:3` runs `wings --config /etc/pelican/config.yml`.\n  - **Ports and volumes:** it exposes 8080 (API) and 2022 (SFTP), and declares volumes for `/etc/pelican`, `/var/lib/pelican` and `/var/log/pelican`.\n  - **Docker socket:** Wings manages game-server containers through the host's Docker daemon, so you have to mount `/var/run/docker.sock` when you run it. A comment in the Dockerfile shows the full `docker run` command.\n- `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`, `build/`, local binaries and config, the Nix files, and the markdown docs from the build context.\n\nI took `golang:1.27` from the `go 1.27.4` line in `go.mod`. I couldn't check that this tag exists, so if it doesn't, pass a different one with `--build-arg GO_VERSION=...`.",
